[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-CONTACT
TITLE: Contact Requirements

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-ERRORS
TITLE: Error Handler Requirements

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-APPLICATION-ERRORS
TITLE: Application Errors

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-35
TITLE: Application Error Name
STATEMENT: >>>
The Application Error Contents SHALL include the error name.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates application error contents. The error name tells the visitor which error occurred.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-36
TITLE: Application Error Description
STATEMENT: >>>
The Application Error Contents SHALL include the error description.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates application error contents. The error description tells the visitor what the error means.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-37
TITLE: Application Error Reference Number
STATEMENT: >>>
The Application Error Contents SHALL include an error reference number.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates application error contents. The reference number associates that instance of the error with backend logging when the error is included in a bug report. This requirement does not set the number's format.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-38
TITLE: Application Error Debugging Information
STATEMENT: >>>
When the visitor is a logged-in administrator, the Application Error Contents SHALL include debugging information.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates debugging information. A logged-in administrator uses that information to diagnose the application error. This requirement does not define that debugging data or how the administrator role is granted.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-HTTP-ERRORS
TITLE: HTTP Errors

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-39
TITLE: HTTP Error Code
STATEMENT: >>>
The HTTP Error Contents SHALL include the error code.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates HTTP error contents. The error code is the HTTP status of the failed response.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-40
TITLE: HTTP Error Name
STATEMENT: >>>
The HTTP Error Contents SHALL include the error name.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates HTTP error contents. The error name tells the visitor which HTTP error occurred.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-41
TITLE: HTTP Error Description
STATEMENT: >>>
The HTTP Error Contents SHALL include the error description.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates HTTP error contents. The error description tells the visitor what the HTTP error means.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-42
TITLE: HTTP Error Request Information
STATEMENT: >>>
When the visitor is a logged-in administrator, the HTTP Error Contents SHALL include the request packet information.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates request information on an HTTP error. A logged-in administrator uses the request packet information to diagnose the failed request. This requirement does not define how that information is captured or how the administrator role is granted.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-43
TITLE: HTTP Error Response Information
STATEMENT: >>>
When the visitor is a logged-in administrator, the HTTP Error Contents SHALL include the response packet information.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates response information on an HTTP error. A logged-in administrator uses the response packet information to diagnose the failed response. This requirement does not define how that information is captured or how the administrator role is granted.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-PAGES
TITLE: Public Pages

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-PAGES-COMMON
TITLE: Common Page Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-44
TITLE: Common Page Header
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless otherwise specified, a public page SHALL include the Header at the top of the page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates placement of the Header. This is the default placement of the Header on a public page. Another requirement may specify otherwise.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-46
TITLE: Common Page Footer
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless otherwise specified, a public page SHALL include the Footer at the bottom of the page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates placement of the Footer. This is the default placement of the Footer on a public page. Another requirement may specify otherwise.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-47
TITLE: Common Page Announcements Bar
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless otherwise specified, a public page SHALL include the Announcements Bar when there is an announcement to display.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Announcements Bar is the Urgent Announcement Container. This requirement places that container on a public page when it has an announcement to display. Another requirement may specify otherwise.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-33
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-48
TITLE: Common Page Errors
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless otherwise specified, a public page SHALL display the error contents when an error occurs.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR allocates how a page presents an error. A public page displays the error contents so the visitor sees the error that occurred. Those contents are the Application Error Contents or the HTTP Error Contents. Another requirement may specify otherwise.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-HOME-PAGE
TITLE: Home Page Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-49
TITLE: Home Page Announcements Display
STATEMENT: >>>
The public home page SHALL include the Announcements Display in place of the Announcements Bar.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
GSSC-PHLR-47 includes the Announcements Bar on a public page unless otherwise specified. This requirement specifies the Announcements Display for the home page. The legacy home page shows announcement text and has no carousel.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-2
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-33
  ROLE: Refines

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-HOME-ANNOUNCEMENTS
