UID: GSSC-PHLR-NEWSLETTERS-PAGE
TITLE: Newsletters Page Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-121
TITLE: Newsletter Selection Form
STATEMENT: >>>
The newsletters page SHALL include a form to select a newsletter.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The legacy newsletters page lists issues by year and month. This requirement gives the page a form for selecting an issue.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-122
TITLE: Newsletter Volume Menu
STATEMENT: >>>
The Newsletter Selection Form SHALL include a menu for the Volume, which is the year of the issue.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Volume menu selects the year of the newsletter. The legacy page groups issues under a year. This requirement does not set the years in the menu.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-123
TITLE: Newsletter Number Menu
STATEMENT: >>>
The Newsletter Selection Form SHALL include a menu for the Number, which is the month of the issue.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Number menu selects the month of the newsletter. The legacy page lists months under each year. This requirement does not set the months in the menu.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-124
TITLE: Selected Newsletter
STATEMENT: >>>
The newsletters page SHALL display the newsletter selected in the Newsletter Selection Form.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The page shows the issue chosen by the Volume and Number menus. The legacy page links to each issue as a separate file. This requirement does not set how the issue is presented.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-10
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PHLR-125
TITLE: Default Newsletter
STATEMENT: >>>
The newsletters page SHALL display the most recent newsletter by default.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Before a visitor selects another issue, the page shows the most recent newsletter. The legacy page also identifies the newest issue separately from the yearly lists.
<<<
